  "Question": "A sign at the fish market says, “\\(50 \\%\\) off, today only: half-pound packages for just \\(\\$3\\) per package.” What is the regular price for a full pound of fish, in dollars?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(6\\)",
    "B": "\\(9\\)",
    "C": "\\(10\\)",
    "D": "\\(12\\)",
    "E": "\\(15\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "A \\(50\\%\\) discount means the sale price is half the regular price. Therefore the regular price of a half-pound package is\n\\[\n3\\div\\frac12=6\\text{ dollars}.\n\\]\nA full pound contains two half-pound packages, so its regular price is\n\\[\n2\\cdot6=\\boxed{12}\\text{ dollars},\n\\]\nchoice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
